@startuml target_hit_miss_sequence
title L0 delivery with optional L1-assisted production
autonumber
actor "Caller" as Caller
participant "_ensure_csrc_cache" as Ensure
participant "Target resolver" as Resolve
participant "_build_csrc_cache\nCPU target container" as Producer
database "GitHub Cache\nL0" as L0
database "OBS\nL1 snapshots" as L1
participant "Existing csrc engine" as Engine
participant "Image / PR nightly consumer" as Consumer

Caller -> Ensure : source ref + Dockerfile OR nightly runtime + SOC
Ensure -> Ensure : resolve immutable source SHA / tracked csrc hash
Ensure -> Resolve : resolve actual environment / architecture targets
Resolve --> Ensure : BuildTarget[]
Ensure -> Producer : source SHA + target + failure tolerance
Producer -> Producer : compute L0 identity in the actual build environment
Producer -> L0 : exact restore
alt L0 valid and compatible
  L0 --> Producer : final artifacts
  Producer -> Producer : skip L1 restore and native compilation
else L0 absent / unavailable / rejected
  Producer -> Producer : discard rejected native outputs before fallback
  Producer -> L1 : restore compatible incremental snapshot
  alt L1 restore available
    L1 --> Producer : incremental entries
  else L1 unavailable / incompatible
    L1 --> Producer : MISS / transport failure
    note right of Producer : Continue with cold compilation.
  end
  Producer -> Engine : install/build with unchanged compiler semantics
  Engine -> Engine : validate individual entries; compile misses
  alt native build succeeds
    Engine -> Engine : prune after success; mark updated state
    Engine --> Producer : final native artifacts
    Producer -> Producer : verify artifacts / record nightly manifest
    Producer -> L0 : save final artifacts using actions/cache
    opt trusted L1 writer credentials and updated cache
      Producer -> L1 : save post-prune snapshot using existing action
    end
  else build fails
    Engine --> Producer : actual build failure
    note right of Producer : Publish no new L0; retain caller fallback.
  end
end
Producer --> Ensure : completed / tolerated producer failure
Ensure --> Caller : pinned source identity
Caller -> Consumer : start original install/build path
Consumer -> L0 : restore same namespace and literal artifact paths
alt matching L0 (nightly: manifest and checksums valid)
  L0 --> Consumer : final artifacts
  Consumer -> Consumer : install package with native compilation disabled
else cache missing / save failed / ref scope differs / validation fails
  Consumer -> Consumer : original source-build fallback
end
note over Caller, Consumer
  Producer success does not guarantee later cache availability.
  Cache transport failures degrade performance; actual product build/test
  failures remain visible. No unconditional test-error retries.
end note
@enduml
